      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "VINCHESKA (7) had to dig deep to salute at the most recent appearance over 2138m at Albion Park, getting home by just a head. Drawn to enjoy an economical run and might sweat on the sprint lane. Meets a comparable field so she is capable of getting the job done again. GREAT WHITE NZ (4) produced a better effort when second up last start, finishing third over 1780m at this track. Tackles a similar assignment and he can go right on with the job. BEYOND DOUBT NZ (5) won two starts ago then things went wrong last start when he copped interference then broke and finished 8 metres away in sixth over 2280m at this track. Must get things right but if he does, a big run is on the cards. MAJOR CRUNCH (8) the best of the rest.",
